{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.QZeroComplexExtension","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.QZeroComplexExtension","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroComplexExtension.complex_q_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroComplexExtension.complex_q_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-zero-complex-extension.lean#L41-L46","doc":"The complement statement on the modulus: `|q| > 1` rules out\n`q = 0` directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroComplexExtension.complex_q_is_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroComplexExtension.complex_q_is_unit","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-zero-complex-extension.lean#L31-L39","doc":"Structural admissibility witness: if `1 < ‖q‖` in `ℂ` then `q`\nis a unit, so the polymorphic substrate identities (Hecke\nquadratic, bar involution, Frobenius pairing, Markov trace)\nspecialize at `R = ℂ` without modification. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-zero-complex-extension","label":"prop:q-zero-complex-extension","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-zero-complex-extension.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}